{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_forecasting_agent", "label": "Forecasting agent design outline", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_reporting_vs_forecasting_split", "label": "Reporting and forecasting are two jobs with opposite failure modes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reporting's failure is a wrong number, forecasting's a confident number; both are computed by code and the agent narrates, diffs and frames a decision."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_tools_compute_agent_narrates", "label": "The agent never does arithmetic", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same question twice gives the same answer; a wrong figure is fixable in one line for everyone; the moment the agent computes a percentage nothing is auditable. Enforced structurally by tests asserting tools agree with the dashboard."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_snapshot_archive", "label": "Snapshot archive: facts packs, scope.json, forecast-log.json", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A dashboard shows state; a report is about change. Without stored facts packs the agent only restates the dashboard, and without the forecast log it is unfalsifiable \u2014 a horoscope."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_reporting_scope_is_not_forecasting_scope", "label": "Reporting scope is not forecasting scope", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The facts pack counts only the reported period; the forecaster sees the whole file. Conflating them produced '89% complete' for a 55% sprint; tests/test_agent.py pins identical delivery figures."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_unit_rule_calendar_vs_working", "label": "Calendar days reported, working days simulated", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Found by a test: facts pack and dashboard disagreed on flow efficiency 25% vs 22% purely on this. Holidays shorten simulated time only; shortening the working week can drop a board under the refusal threshold, and the refusal is the right output."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_monte_carlo_item_throughput", "label": "Monte Carlo over item throughput, 20,000 seeded trials", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Six sprints give six point-observations but sixty items; zero-throughput days stay in the sample or the model never predicts a stall; fixed seed; scope growth sampled from scope.json and stated inline when absent."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_recommend_commitment_85", "label": "Commitment recommended at the 85%-confidence item count", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Committing at the median misses half the time by construction and a team that misses half its commitments stops being believed; 11 items vs a median of 14 on the sample."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_size_stability_guard", "label": "size_stability: drift and spread guard on item counting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Splitting work smaller raises throughput without output rising; a 30% cycle-time fall with a 20% throughput rise means splitting; p85/p50 above ~4 means items are not interchangeable. Forecasts marked provisional, never switched back to points."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_refusal_thresholds", "label": "Refusal thresholds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Completion forecast >=10 completed items and >=8 day-observations, named separately with units; cycle-time risk >=6 items; calibration >=10 resolved; reference class >=5 epics; t-shirt >=8; explicit min<=likely<=max; sequencing >=2 sizeable asks."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_intake_sizing_ladder", "label": "Intake sizing ladder: tshirt, reference-class, explicit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rung is always declared and each prints its own caveat; two scenarios (earliest possible, realistic with queue and thinned throughput) always both, the difference reported as the cost of the queue in working days."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_uncertainty_attribution", "label": "Uncertainty attributed to size vs delivery variability", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three simulations (both varying, size frozen, throughput frozen) split the spread; size-driven sends the ask back to refinement, delivery-driven says the estimate was never the problem. 54% vs 10% on the demo."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_sequencing_consequences_not_score", "label": "Sequencing returns consequences, never a score", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything missing its date in every ordering is reported first; no WSJF or weighted score because they multiply two unvalidated estimates and present the product as arithmetic."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_guardrails", "label": "Agent guardrails", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never compute; never a single date; lead with probability against the reader's date; evidence tags; never attribute throughput to a person; never recommend longer hours; movement is the news; stale data first; publish the Brier score and stop above 0.20; never rank asks; an intake figure is never a commitment."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_backtest_non_overlapping", "label": "Backtest with non-overlapping windows and full horizons", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only score cutoffs with a full horizon of real data (truncation made p50 coverage read 38%); never overlap windows (one slow fortnight counted ten times). Six windows is a smoke test, not calibration."}, {"id": "docs_forecasting_agent_brier_score", "label": "Brier score over the forecast log", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Target <=0.12; above 0.20 the agent stops publishing probabilities in the body."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_reporting_vs_forecasting_split", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_tools_compute_agent_narrates", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_snapshot_archive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_reporting_scope_is_not_forecasting_scope", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_unit_rule_calendar_vs_working", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_monte_carlo_item_throughput", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_recommend_commitment_85", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-agent.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_forecasting_agent", "target": "docs_forecasting_agent_size_stability_guard", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/forecasting-a